# Detection Algorithm Development

All fret-press detection logic and actuation timing are developed **on the PC side** in `tools/fret-tuner/` (Python). The firmware (`firmware/fretboard/`) only scans ADCs, streams raw data, and receives GPIO bitmask commands — do not add detection or actuation logic there.

## Firmware Is Read-Only

- Do **not** modify firmware source files for detection work
- The firmware modules `fret_detect.c` and `fret_button.c` are inactive legacy code; their PC-side equivalents are `detect_*.py` and `actuator.py`

## Per-detector constraints

The fret-tuner tool itself imposes no portability constraints. Some individual detectors carry their own per-file constraints (for example M0+ portability targets noted in their module docstrings); treat those as **detector-local**, not tool-wide. New detectors are free to use any PC-side facility (NumPy, OpenCV, etc.) unless their own header says otherwise.
